CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ converted through the deduced type: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
static assertion failed
--
Class template argument deduction required every template parameter to be
deduced, so with an undeducible defaulted parameter it fell back to taking
the argument type as C (view<const char *>).  GCC 11's
std::filesystem::path(const Source &) lost its body this way
(__effective_range returns `basic_string_view{&*__source}').
